## Detection Engineering & Configuration

### 1. Custom Correlation Rules (`detections/local_rules.xml`)
To eliminate alert noise from isolated user errors while catching automated credential stuffing/brute-force bursts, a two-tier rule hierarchy was deployed:
* **Rule `100010` (Level 6):** Child of Rule `30318`; isolates anomalous authentication requests targeting `login.php`.
* **Rule `100011` (Level 12):** Frequency-based correlation rule (`frequency="8"`, `timeframe="30"`, `<same_srcip />`) mapped to **MITRE ATT&CK `T1110.001`**.

*(See full XML implementation in [`./detections/local_rules.xml`](./detections/local_rules.xml))*

### 2. Automated Containment (`configs/ossec-active-response.xml`)
Configured in `/var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf` on `wazuh-server` to execute `firewall-drop` locally on the targeted endpoint (`location="local"`) whenever Rule `100011` fires, enforcing a 120-second network block (`timeout="120"`).

*(See configuration snippet in [`./configs/ossec-active-response.xml`](./configs/ossec-active-response.xml))*

