## Verification & Validation Commands

The following commands were used during lab execution to validate rule syntax, monitor real-time containment, and inspect active firewall rules on the target host (`jeanpubuntu`):

```bash
# 1. Validate custom Wazuh rule syntax and restart Wazuh Manager (on wazuh-server)
sudo /var/ossec/bin/wazuh-analysisd -t
sudo systemctl restart wazuh-manager

# 2. Monitor Active Response execution (add/delete actions) on Ubuntu Target
sudo tail -f /var/ossec/logs/active-responses.log

# 3. Inspect dynamic iptables DROP rule during the 120-second containment window
sudo iptables -L -n -v | grep 192.168.140.148
```

