## Preventive Hardening Recommendations

While Wazuh Active Response provides rapid reactive containment at the network layer, defense-in-depth requires layered application and host-level controls (detailed in Section 6 of the full PDF report):
* **Application Hardening:** Transition DVWA from *Low* to *High/Impossible* security levels to enforce strict server-side session validation and input sanitization.
* **Anti-CSRF Tokens & Rate Limiting:** Require single-use `user_token` validation on login forms alongside progressive back-off delays.
* **Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA):** Enforce TOTP or FIDO2 authentication on exposed administrative and user portals.
* **Reverse Proxy / WAF:** Place containerized web applications behind Nginx rate-limiting (`limit_req_zone`) or ModSecurity (OWASP CRS).

